    "preheader": "NIFTY 50 fell 0.63% to 25,227.95 as metal and IT shares declined; foreign investors bought ₹5,867 crore (provisional); Fed minutes pointed to further rate rises.",
    "subject": "Kubeerra Market Brief · Thu 19 Nov: NIFTY 50 ends 0.63% lower at 25,227.95; metals fall 2.46%"
  },
  "brief": [
    "The NIFTY 50 fell 0.63% to 25,227.95 and the Sensex 0.61% to 82,031.81 on Wednesday as investors booked profits after November's gains; Nifty Bank fell 0.38% to 62,038.65 (HDFC Sky, Marketcalls).",
    "Nifty Metal fell 2.46% and Nifty IT 1.24%; the NIFTY Midcap 100 fell 1.22% and the Smallcap 100 about 0.35% (Marketcalls, Kotak Neo).",
    "Foreign investors bought a net ₹5,867 crore and domestic institutions sold a net ₹3,160 crore (provisional, Kotak Neo). The rupee rose 7 paise to 93.44 per dollar (PTI).",
    "Overseas, the Dow fell 1.11%, led by health insurers, and the S&P 500 0.23% while the Nasdaq rose 0.42%; Fed minutes showed almost all officials saw further rate rises as likely (Closing Look, The Motley Fool, Reuters).",
    "IBJA's afternoon rates on Wednesday put gold at ₹1,31,164 per 10 g and silver at ₹1,63,733 per kg, down ₹3,037 and ₹5,438 on the day (IBJA)."
  ],
